## L7. What away says of the spare
-- an Antigravity spare, listening as it should:
$ (the operator, at a terminal, answering y) handoff away one
    Cover: the spare can take any seat that gets stuck while you're away. Turn cover on? [y/N] y
    Cover: on. The spare can take a seat that gets stuck while you're away; you'll be told if it does.
    the spare isn't told: it holds no work
    The spare is an Antigravity session: it listens with a wait it runs in the background. If it stops running one, handoff can wake it only 10 times before you type in it.
-- the same spare at its cap:
$ (the operator, at a terminal, answering y) handoff away two
